    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d78">

                <pb facs="0157" n="125" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v06/pg125"/>

                <head>78. Telegram From the Embassy in Cuba to the Department of State<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d78-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Havana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1958-07-03T09:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 3, 1958—9
                                a.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>18. Briefly these are facts. Consul Wollam believes everybody well. Conditions
                    for release are: <list>
                        <label>(A)</label>
                        <item>No more shipment of arms.</item>
                        <label>(B)</label>
                        <item>Complete assurance that naval base will not be used for supplying arms
                            and munitions.</item>
                        <label>(C)</label>
                        <item>An observer to assure compliance with MDAP agreement.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>Wollam states that these people are fanatics with blind spots and determined.
                    Wollam says he is sure there are Communists in the group but mixed up in
                    thinking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Smith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
